Why GPL-3.0-or-later
--------------------

SleepRadioPi's Broadcast Radio auto-DJ mode uses on-device text-to-speech via
sherpa-onnx (https://github.com/k2-fsa/sherpa-onnx), via its Python bindings.
sherpa-onnx itself is Apache-2.0, but for Piper / VITS voices it statically
links eSpeak-NG (https://github.com/espeak-ng/espeak-ng) for phoneme
generation, and eSpeak-NG is licensed GPL-3.0-or-later. Because a running
install therefore includes GPL-licensed code, the project as a whole is
distributed under GPL-3.0-or-later.

Corresponding source is this repository:
https://github.com/dylan7474/SleepRadioPi

This project is a from-scratch Python reimplementation of the ideas and
algorithms in the Android app SleepRadio (https://github.com/dylan7474/SleepRadio,
also GPL-3.0-or-later), targeting a standalone Raspberry Pi device instead of
a phone. See docs/SCOPE.md for the relationship between the two projects.


Third-party components (planned)
---------------------------------

* sherpa-onnx .......... Apache-2.0         https://github.com/k2-fsa/sherpa-onnx
* eSpeak-NG ............ GPL-3.0-or-later   https://github.com/espeak-ng/espeak-ng
    (statically linked inside sherpa-onnx's native library; also the source of
     the espeak-ng-data phoneme files installed at runtime)

Other planned dependencies (python-vlc / libVLC, mutagen, numpy, sounddevice,
gpiozero, a small LCD driver library) are permissively licensed (LGPL/MIT/BSD
family) and do not change the overall GPL-3.0-or-later status, which is
already fixed by the eSpeak-NG dependency above. Re-check this file if the
dependency list changes.
